 "novel": {
  "pour-cup-refills-after-empty": "Glass pouring cup is visibly empty and inverted 8.5-9.5 s, then shows green olive content at 9.75 s with no refill. Reported by core-s1, core-s2, core-s3, router-s1 (4 layers). Frames 35-40 confirm empty cup at 8.5-9.5 and a green olive-like mass in the cup at 9.75 (at frame edge, last frame, so moderate confidence).",
  "steel-bowl-olives-regrow": "After the scoop leaves ~1-2 green olives in the steel bowl (5.25 s), the green count rises to ~3 (6.0-6.75 s) and ~5 (8.25-9.75 s) with nothing added. Reported by router-s1, router-s2 (x2), router-s3 (x2); core-s1 object-persistence|1 also mentions it but was classed OLIV-4 for its main claim. Frames 22/25/28/34/36/40 confirm the increase, though camera angle shifts between 5.25 and 6.0 s."
 },
 "lenient": [
  "core-s1|man-cups|spatial-topology-occlusion|0: cups re-forming diamond->row mapped to CUPS-3 (cup count/arrangement), following prior argon TP for 'staggered cups align into a straight row'",
  "core-s2|man-cups|baseline-generalist|2: same diamond->row arrangement claim, CUPS-3 per argon precedent",
  "core-s2|man-cups|spatial-topology-occlusion|0: same diamond->row arrangement claim, CUPS-3 per argon precedent",
  "router-s2|man-cups|possession-tracking|0: framed as stack->single silver coin (quantity drop), so CUPS-3 like argon's center-cup-coins-vanish; colour-only variants were FP (qwen precedent)",
  "core-s1|man-cups|baseline-generalist|2: coins-on-centre-vanish part = CUPS-3; the beige-centre morph part alone would be FP",
  "core-s1|pouring-olives|object-persistence-state|2: dark olives appearing in the cup on the second pour mapped to OLIV-1 (argon's OLIV-1 TP explicitly covered the second pour); same for all second-pour dark-olive findings",
  "router-s2|pouring-olives|possession-tracking|1: jar colour mix after 2nd pour too dark -> OLIV-1 (colour) rather than OLIV-2 (volume); same for router-s3 count-stability|2",
  "core-s3|pouring-olives|object-persistence-state|3: brown items appearing in steel bowl after the scoop mapped to OLIV-4 (argon_v1-s3 TP described the bowl turning into brown items); same for router-s1 possession|3, router-s3 possession|3, router-s3 pour|4, core-s2 baseline|2",
  "core-s1|child-marbles|object-persistence-state|1: ball count dropping 9->~5 at 5.75 s (verified in frames: right half of bowl empty) mapped to MARB-1 'heavy morphing while stirring'; same for core-s2 baseline|0, core-s3 baseline|0, router-s2 possession|0, router-s3 count|2, possession|1, pour|0",
  "core-s1|child-marbles|baseline-generalist|1: shape-only morph claims (lumpy/blob balls) mapped to MARB-1's 'heavy morphing while stirring', following argon_v1-s2 TP; hand-ball merge claims kept FP (motion blur)"
 ],
 "notes": "man-cups: no Opus finding for CUPS-2 (coin->cup) or CUPS-5 (six fingers). Colour-only claims on the middle-cup top coin (gold->silver) are FP per qwen precedent; claims of stack level dropping/emptying are CUPS-3 per argon precedent. Coin-inscription pseudo-text/morph claims (router text-stability, 7 findings) classed FP: legends are tiny and out of focus, readings are resolution-limited and not verifiable (unlike the large garbled diner sign). Flag to KT if they want coin text treated like garbled sign text. Audience-vanishing claim is FP: the camera orbits ~180 deg, so the later background is the opposite side of the room. Facial-hair growth FP (hair micro-morph class). Hover/never-released coin claims FP (argon precedent). child-marbles: torso/beige-panel claim FP (beige between the arms is already visible at 8.25 s; camera push-in puts the torso out of frame). Hovering balls on the far wall are FP (motion-blurred mid-bounce). pouring-olives: handheld vessel shape change (router-s1 pour|5) FP, since it is the same glass tumbler seen at different tilts."
}